## What the licence does NOT cover

Two files in this repository are **third-party code, vendored verbatim** and
are not mine to license:

    src/pitvis/evaluation/official.py
    src/pitvis/evaluation/official_instruments.py

They are the PitVis-2023 challenge organisers' own scoring scripts, copied
byte-for-byte from `helper_scripts/` in <https://github.com/dreets/pitvis> at
the commits and sha256 digests recorded in each file's header. Only a docstring
was prepended; no line of the original body was changed.

They are reproduced here for a specific and narrow reason: this project's
headline numbers are computed by calling those functions directly, so the
scores it reports are the challenge's scores **by construction** rather than by
reimplementation. A reader can verify that claim without trusting it.

**The upstream repository publishes no licence**, so no rights in those two
files are granted by this repository, and the AGPL grant above does not extend
to them. If you intend to reuse them, obtain permission from their authors.

